{"name":"Base Camp","hex":"#575c3a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"base camp","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An encampment used temporarily for storing supplies and preparing for a larger activity (especially one at a higher altitude or farther afield), such as mountain climbing or hunting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/base_camp"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mountaineering","blocks":[{"text":"Mountaineering is a set of outdoor activities that involves ascending mountains. Mountaineering-related activities include traditional outdoor climbing, skiing, and traversing via ferratas that have become sports in their own right. Indoor climbing, sport climbing, and bouldering are also considered variants of mountaineering by some, but are part of a wide group of mountain sports. In everyday language, the term \"mountaineering\" is synonymous with mountain climbing or alpinism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/M_Rainier.jpg/330px-M_Rainier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountaineering","wikidata":"Q36908"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Edward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg/500px-Edward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Edward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg/1280px-Edward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Edward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg/500px-Edward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Edward Whymper (1840–1911), painting by Lance Calkin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEdward_Whymper_Calkin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Leontopodium_alpinum_1.JPG/500px-Leontopodium_alpinum_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Leontopodium_alpinum_1.JPG/500px-Leontopodium_alpinum_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Edelweiss, a plant associated with mountain sports","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeontopodium_alpinum_1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/WilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg/500px-WilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/WilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg/1280px-WilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/WilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg/500px-WilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"British mountaineer William Cecil Slingsby became known as the father of Norwegian mountaineering and contributed greatly to its popularization with his classic book Norway, the Northern Playground.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilliamCecilSlingsby_Storen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Owen_Glynne_Jones_12_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Owen_Glynne_Jones_12_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Owen_Glynne_Jones_12_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Owen_Glynne_Jones_12_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Owen_Glynne_Jones_12_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Owen_Glynne_Jones_12_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu